{
  "rationale": "Iteration 0 has no race data, so this is a conservative baseline built from the contract's ranges. Geometry: five line sensors spread across 0.04 m (x = -0.02 to +0.02 m, 0.01 m spacing) at y = 0.03 m ahead of the axle. A 12 mm footprint is about half the 25 mm tape width, so the sensors see the line on a bend without losing it. The 0.12 m track and 0.03 m wheel radius are mid-range for stable yaw response. Mass 0.8 kg and body 0.18 x 0.12 m keep inertia moderate, and body_width 0.12 m gives an off-track allowance of max(0.06, 0.0125 + 0.03) = 0.06 m. Controller: base_speed 1.6 (about 80 percent of full PWM) to reach roughly 1.5 m/s average and finish under 3 s. Weights -2 to +2 are antisymmetric so the signal is zero when the line is centred. kp 2.5 gives a moderate steering authority. ki 0.1 is small to remove any left/right motor-mismatch bias without windup. kd 0.1 damps the sway. line_loss 'last_direction' keeps the robot turning toward the line it last saw. Expected result: completion on the oval and s-bend, with rms_error under about 0.03 m. The main risk is overshoot on the slalom, which would show up as high steering_oscillation and max_error. Next measurements: whether the run completes, its completion_time, and whether the max_error and oscillation fall within the allowed off-track distance.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": -0.01, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": 0.01, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.03}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.18,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.6,
    "kp": 2.5,
    "ki": 0.1,
    "kd": 0.1,
    "sensor_weights": [-2.0, -1.0, 0.0, 1.0, 2.0],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": ["completion", "progress", "completion_time", "rms_error", "max_error", "line_loss_events", "steering_oscillation"]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor robot",
      "notes": "Baseline candidate from contract ranges with no race data yet: five 12 mm sensors at 0.01 m spacing, base_speed 1.6, kp 2.5, ki 0.1, kd 0.1, and last_direction line recovery. Expected to complete with low rms_error; the main risk is slalom overshoot."
    }
  }
}
